  "presentation_summary": [
    "67-year-old man developed lower-leg numbness and weakness that spread to upper limbs; MRI showed multiple lacunar infarctions.",
    "He had hypertension, multiple mononeuropathy, anemia, renal dysfunction, and high CRP before sudden severe right flank pain.",
    "At transfer his blood pressure was 192/114 mmHg, pulse 98/min, and temperature 37.1 C.",
    "Admission labs showed hemoglobin 6.2 g/dL, WBC 13.61 x10^9/L, platelets 321 x10^9/L, BUN 39 mg/dL, creatinine 1.3 mg/dL, ESR 156 mm/h, and CRP 11.5 mg/dL.",
    "Contrast CT showed bilateral pleural effusion, small right renal infarction, and right perirenal hematoma; CTA/angiography found multiple renal and splenic microaneurysms, with selective coil embolization of the bleeding renal aneurysm."
  ],
